collect elements from streams into list

If you’re talking about Java Streams, you collect elements into a List using a terminal operation.

Basic example
List<String> list = stream.collect(Collectors.toList());

Since Java 16 (recommended)
List<String> list = stream.toList();


Returns an unmodifiable list
Cleaner and preferred for most cases
With filtering and mapping
List<Integer> result = numbers.stream()
        .filter(n -> n > 10)
        .map(n -> n * 2)
        .toList();

If you need a mutable list
List<String> list = stream.collect(Collectors.toCollection(ArrayList::new));

From an array
List<String> list = Arrays.stream(array).toList();

From a collection
List<String> list = collection.stream().toList();

Summary
Approach	                                Mutable             	        Java Version
stream.toList()	                                 ❌                         	16+
Collectors.toList()	                        ⚠️ (implementation-dependent)	     8+
Collectors.toCollection(ArrayList::new)      	✅	                             8+

